{"ts":"2026-11-15T01:09:07.970Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"The classic gravity-tunnel result in the stated idealisation (said aloud: 'forget air, heat and rock'; footnote: uniform, non-rotating Earth, no air). Inputs from NASA's Earth Fact Sheet: R = 6,371 km, GM = 398,600 km^3/s^2. One way pi*sqrt(R^3/GM) = 2,530 s = 42.2 min ('about 42'); v_max = sqrt(GM/R) = 7.91 km/s = 28,475 km/h ('about 28,000'); a grazing orbit 2*pi*sqrt(R^3/GM) = 84.3 min, half of it equal to the drop. Chord independence holds for a uniform sphere (the along-tunnel component of gravity is proportional to the distance from the chord midpoint, with the same omega). 'Exactly' applies within the model. Real-Earth density raises it to ~38 min; I don't claim a real-Earth figure."},"gitSha":"910e1db"}
